            {
                "entry_id": "87eef13f-a11d-30d3-bcb2-de955838e8f2",
                "word": "félonie",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "5211493a-0e6d-4e5c-8b64-c2acea9f331a",
                        "entry_id": "87eef13f-a11d-30d3-bcb2-de955838e8f2",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "félonies"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "62e98198-7700-374b-9e71-67142b9d472b",
                        "entry_id": "87eef13f-a11d-30d3-bcb2-de955838e8f2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Sentiments ou manière d’agir d’un vassal félon vis-à-vis de son seigneur."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "dd54db44-9505-4305-ad94-a5282c360c7d",
                                "sense_id": "62e98198-7700-374b-9e71-67142b9d472b",
                                "text": "La félonie de Ganelon."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4d67a1ce-4ce9-43d8-8c2d-a24afe145c11",
                                "sense_id": "62e98198-7700-374b-9e71-67142b9d472b",
                                "text": "Être coupable, convaincu de félonie."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9ff96134-9ffc-33a5-ae93-03b9fd8ee13a",
                        "entry_id": "87eef13f-a11d-30d3-bcb2-de955838e8f2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Déloyauté."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "broadly"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e3abfeff-7ef3-4595-857c-37ae3c7cbcdb",
                                "sense_id": "9ff96134-9ffc-33a5-ae93-03b9fd8ee13a",
                                "text": "Angèle. — Vous ne vous êtes donc pas dit que vous commettiez là une horrible félonie !\nThommereux. — Oh ! Si, je me le suis dit… Je me le suis dit… dix fois.. vingt fois…\nAngèle. — Eh ! bien ?\nThommereux. — Eh ! bien ! à la vingtième… J’y étais habitué !"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4b1a08a4-b522-4479-88a2-0d31b24fd504",
                                "sense_id": "9ff96134-9ffc-33a5-ae93-03b9fd8ee13a",
                                "text": "Il est là. Il fume paisiblement une cigarette, une cigarette du paquet que je lui ai donné… Mon Dieu ! pardonnez-moi cette félonie."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "341009bc-f430-46f2-a6ce-50c69ad0e2b5",
                                "sense_id": "9ff96134-9ffc-33a5-ae93-03b9fd8ee13a",
                                "text": "Pour accuser avec une telle assurance, il fallait qu'existât la preuve indéniable de la félonie de François."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c90f357c-1064-4026-a54d-4148818a613d",
                                "sense_id": "9ff96134-9ffc-33a5-ae93-03b9fd8ee13a",
                                "text": "[Cela se passait à] l'âge chevaleresque où, pour croire à la parole de l'homme, il n'était pas besoin de l'inscrire dans un contrat ; où l'on ne connaissait pas un plus grand bien en ce monde que l'honneur intact, pas une plus grande honte que la félonie."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bbb563a1-10a8-4193-81b9-5667fce1b1c3",
                        "source_entry_id": "87eef13f-a11d-30d3-bcb2-de955838e8f2",
                        "target_lang_word": "treason",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "treason",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9db7b9e5-1dd1-3ab4-a782-86dd643eb0e9",
                                        "entry_id": "082937ed-ca24-3bd6-9baa-8e5c05ab9dce",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The crime of betraying one’s own country."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b26e92cb-c38a-449f-9341-a1fe73d11d2d",
                                                "sense_id": "9db7b9e5-1dd1-3ab4-a782-86dd643eb0e9",
                                                "text": "Treaſon doth never [pro]ſper: what's the reaſon? / For yf yt [pro]ſper none dare call yt treaſon"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b8a0fdf6-1484-4d1a-9106-80198bc0a467",
                                                "sense_id": "9db7b9e5-1dd1-3ab4-a782-86dd643eb0e9",
                                                "text": "Treason against the United States, shall consist only in levying War against them, or in adhering to their Enemies, giving them Aid and Comfort. No Person shall be convicted of Treason unleſs on the Testimony of two Witneſses to the same overt Act, or on Confeſsion in open Court."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6fae402c-9f0b-4bbf-8dc5-958c5cc6c14e",
                                                "sense_id": "9db7b9e5-1dd1-3ab4-a782-86dd643eb0e9",
                                                "text": "If for every error and every act of incompetence one can substitute an act of treason, many points of fascinating interpretation are open to the paranoid imagination: treason in high places can be found at almost every turning."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "96842da8-fa3f-4235-96ba-77731983f198",
                                                "sense_id": "9db7b9e5-1dd1-3ab4-a782-86dd643eb0e9",
                                                "text": "M. Vonel: 'Your involvement with a group calling themselves THE ORDER OF THE EZIC STAR has been uncovered. […] At least one EZIC member has confessed to receiving your help. This represents treason of the highest order. Goodbye inspector.'"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d745db41-536c-30b3-bd9c-104bb7f503af",
                                        "entry_id": "082937ed-ca24-3bd6-9baa-8e5c05ab9dce",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An act of treachery, betrayal of trust or confidence."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
